WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.190
Weighed recipes: chin chin, puff-puff, meat pie and bread.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.210
This is the video for module two of Basic Baking and Snacks Production.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:19.590
Professional bakers weigh. A cup of flour can weigh anywhere from about 120 g to 160 g, depending on how you scoop it.

4
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.110
That difference is enough to turn soft dough into hard dough.

5
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.800
So weigh everything in grams, every time, and your tenth batch will taste like your first.

6
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:40.050
Before you mix, weigh each ingredient into its own bowl and line them up. Chefs call this mise en place, everything in its place.

7
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.100
Mix 500 g of flour with 100 g of sugar, nutmeg and a pinch of salt.

8
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:54.410
Rub in 100 g of cold margarine with your fingertips, until it looks like fine breadcrumbs.

9
00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:02.910
Beat one egg into the milk and add it a little at a time, until the dough is firm and smooth. You may not need all the milk.

10
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.320
Rest the dough for 10 minutes, then roll it to about 5 mm thick.

11
00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:20.790
Cut pieces the same size so they cook evenly. Fry in small batches with the oil at about 160 to 170 degrees Celsius, until evenly golden.

12
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:30.190
Drain on paper and let it cool completely before you pack it in airtight bags. Too much flour or too little fat makes it rock hard.

13
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:46.100
For puff-puff, beat 500 g of flour, sugar, salt and one 7 g sachet of yeast with lukewarm water for 3 to 5 minutes. Cover it in a warm place for 45 to 60 minutes, until doubled and bubbly.

14
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:52.440
Fry small balls at about 170 to 180 degrees, and serve the same day.

15
00:01:53.690 --> 00:02:05.660
Do not crowd the pot. Each piece cools the oil, and the snack soaks up oil. For example, Ngozi fries her double batch about 10 at a time. Never leave hot oil unattended.

16
00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:14.780
Meat pie sells at a higher price. Cook the minced beef and onion until no pink remains, then add potatoes and carrots.

17
00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:23.440
Thicken it with flour and water, spread it on a tray to cool, and refrigerate it if you will not use it within 2 hours.

18
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:32.710
For the pastry, use 500 g of flour and 250 g of cold margarine. The fat is half the flour weight.

19
00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:41.360
Rub in the fat and add cold water. Do not knead, or the pastry turns hard. Chill the dough for about 20 minutes.

20
00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:53.940
Fill with cold filling, seal with a fork, brush with egg, and bake at about 180 to 200 degrees for 25 to 35 minutes, until the base is golden.

21
00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:59.680
Hot filling makes a soggy base, and raw meat may not reach a safe temperature in the oven.

22
00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:06.760
For example, Hauwa in Kaduna gets an order for 60 meat pies. Her recipe makes 12.

23
00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.020
She finds one factor: 60 divided by 12 is 5.

24
00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:24.750
She multiplies every ingredient by 5. Flour, 500 g times 5, is 2,500 g. Margarine is 1,250 g.

25
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.580
She adds about 10% extra to cover breakages and a tasting sample.

26
00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:38.570
And she mixes in two or three smaller batches, because a huge batch warms up and is hard to rub in evenly.

27
00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:49.000
Bread shows every step. Knead for 10 to 15 minutes, until a small piece stretches thin enough to let light through. That is the windowpane test.

28
00:03:50.250 --> 00:04:01.210
For example, Grace in Port Harcourt bakes her first loaf. Her four tasters score texture 2 out of 5. Heavy and tight. Her notes show she kneaded for only 5 minutes.

29
00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:07.430
She changes one thing only. She kneads for 12 minutes, with a windowpane test.

30
00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.250
Texture rises to 3.5. Now tasters say it is a little pale.

31
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:21.940
Next time she bakes 5 minutes longer, and appearance rises from 3 to 4. One change at a time shows what worked.

32
00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:31.260
So remember. Weigh everything in grams. Cool chin chin fully before packing. Fry in small batches at the right temperature.

33
00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:37.480
Cook the meat filling fully and cool it before filling. And scale every recipe with one factor.

34
00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:48.030
Your practice: fry and record one batch, bake meat pies or a pound cake, write a recipe scaled for 50 pieces, and run a tasting panel.

35
00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.530
Now continue with the lessons below.
